    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear anchor, boasting our highest efficiency score of 83.29. The matchup against Hughes is exceptionally favorable, with a high SP_xERA of 4.72 and significant park and platoon advantages pushing his ceiling higher. Following closely is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (72.48), both of whom benefit from positive matchups against right-handed pitching. **Drake Baldwin** is a surprisingly high-leverage start today (67.77); his spot at the top of the order and a favorable 4.43 xERA opposing pitcher suggest he is primed for R and RBI production, making him a high-efficiency play despite the lower base projection.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Jackson Merrill** (59.93) and **Miguel Vargas** (59.60), who both narrowly edged out our bench options. **Jackson Merrill** faces the toughest test of the day against Lodolo; despite the 4.73 xERA, the left-on-left disadvantage suppressed his score significantly. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (49.45) serves as our most concerning start; while his raw talent is elite, the matchup against a high-tier arm like Williams (2.97 xERA) creates a \"Below floor\" risk profile that nearly saw him relegated to the bench. We are managing a depleted bench due to the ongoing IL stints of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, which necessitates pushing marginal starters like **Tommy White** (48.77) and **Wade Meckler** (43.47) into the lineup to preserve our remaining game caps.\n\nWe are monitoring the **Henry Bolte** (54.06) situation closely; while his speed is vital for our pursuit of SB, the matchup against Gore (3.79 xERA) is suboptimal, and any late-breaking lineup changes could force us to pivot toward depth pieces like **Nasim Nunez** or **Heliot Ramos** if they are confirmed for action. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains our most glaring absence, and his continued unavailability necessitates a cautious approach with our depth players such as **Coby Mayo** and **Curtis Mead**. With the scarcity of steals as our primary concern, we are betting that the combined speed of **Sam Antonacci** and **Gunnar Henderson** will provide enough categorical lift to offset the potential stagnation from our bottom-order bats.",
